.TH SPRITETEXT 1
.SH NAME
spritetext \- read a sprite as text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/spritetext
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I SpriteText
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/SpriteText.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A sprite is a queue of drawing elements, and this walks one twice: first
printing a one-line summary of every element, then listing the whole
thing as the code that would rebuild it.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B up / down
Scroll
.TP
.B "any other key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/spritetext.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR spriteedit (1),
.IR wm (1)
